# Generated files and merges (GF-03) — see
# knowledge/product/governance/kyberion-development-practices.md "Generated files and merges".
#
# linguist-generated collapses these in GitHub diffs. merge=kyberion-regenerate
# uses the repo-local driver that `pnpm install` registers
# (scripts/install_git_merge_driver.mjs → scripts/git_merge_regenerate.mjs);
# where the driver is not configured (GitHub web UI, CI) git falls back to its
# normal text merge. After a merge, run `pnpm kyberion resolve generated`.
docs/developer/CONFIGURATION.md linguist-generated=true merge=kyberion-regenerate
docs/developer/env.example linguist-generated=true merge=kyberion-regenerate
docs/developer/role-assumption-reachability.json linguist-generated=true merge=kyberion-regenerate
knowledge/_index.md linguist-generated=true merge=kyberion-regenerate
# Curated + generated: the driver merges entries by name and only leaves a
# conflict when the same entry changed on both sides. Not linguist-generated —
# its descriptions are reviewed by hand.
knowledge/product/governance/env-registry.json merge=kyberion-regenerate
